      "itemDescription": "One of the country\u2019s largest aerospace and defense manufacturers saw a 7% increase in revenue in 2022, a steady gain as it looks to recover from a drop in revenue in 2019 and 2020 due to the pandemic and widespread groundings of Boeing 737 MAXs.<br />\r\n<ul><br />\r\n \t<li>Order backlog for the company\u2019s commercial airplanes grew in 2022 to $330 billion, from $297 billion a year earlier, partially reflecting increased demand as domestic and international travel rebounded.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>Supply-chain and quality-control issues in 2022 and 2023 have bedeviled Boeing, including the recent halt of some 737 MAX deliveries due to fuselage deficiencies.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>The aerospace and defense manufacturer is reconfiguring its workforce of 156,000 in 2023, planning to cut 2,000 jobs in its finance and human resources departments while intending to hire 10,000 new employees with a focus on tech and manufacturing.</li><br />\r\n</ul>",
      "uri": "/ranking/fortune500/2023/",
      "__typename": "_ItemRankingListsType"
